  "cut_point": "We are told that a **three-digit number** multiplied by **7** yields a product where the digits **following the thousands place** are **638**.\n\nLet’s denote the three-digit number as **N**.\n\nSo, we are told:\n\n$$\n7N = \\text{some 7-digit number with digits 638 followed by some digits}\n$$",
