    "error_reason": "Since N is a three-digit number, 7N is at most 6993, so it cannot be a 7-digit number. Also, \"digits following the thousands place are 638\" means the hundreds, tens, and ones digits are 638, not that the product starts with 638.",
    "new_direction": "Write the product as 1000a + 638, where a is the thousands digit, and find the digit a that makes (1000a + 638)/7 a three-digit integer."
